### 16.2 Full Business Model Canvas (Detailed)

#### **1. Customer Segments**

**Primary:**
- **Mid-size airlines** (50-150 narrowbody aircraft)
  - Coastal route exposure (Mediterranean, Caribbean, North Sea, Southeast Asia)
  - Dust/desert exposure (Middle East, North Africa, Australia inland)
  - Using AMOS, Ramco, or AVIATAR (integration ease)
  
**Secondary:**
- **MRO service providers** (value-add to airline customers)
- **Lessors** (asset health monitoring for portfolio management)

**Tertiary (Future):**
- **Major network carriers** (Year 2-3, after proof)
- **Insurers** (underwriting data for risk assessment)

---

#### **2. Value Propositions**

**Core Promise:**
> "Reduce unplanned maintenance costs by 15-25% through environmental exposure-based predictive maintenance—without changing your existing workflows."

**Specific Value Drivers:**

| **Stakeholder** | **Job to be Done** | **Pain Relieved** | **Gain Created** |
|----------------|-------------------|------------------|------------------|
| **Maintenance Planner** | Optimize wash/inspect schedules | Calendar-based = wasteful OR risky | Risk-based scheduling, explainable |
| **Tech Ops Manager** | Minimize AOG events | Surprises ground aircraft | Early warnings, predictability |
| **Finance Director** | Control costs | Budget overruns from unplanned work | Measurable savings (IATA categories) |
| **Reliability Engineer** | Improve fleet health | Lack of environmental data | Exposure visibility, root cause |
| **Sustainability Lead** | ESG reporting | No environmental impact data | Contrail + exposure quantification |

**Differentiation vs. Competitors:**
- ✅ **vs. Skywise/AVIATAR**: Specialized environmental focus they don't have
- ✅ **vs. RR/GE**: OEM-neutral, works across all engines
- ✅ **vs. Satavia**: Maintenance ROI focus, not just climate
- ✅ **vs. ACSIS/Forge**: Environmental exposure angle unique
- ✅ **vs. Generic PdM**: Aviation-specific, proven datasets (ERA5/CAMS)

